e qu’une armure lourde.</p>\n<h2>Place dans la création de personnage</h2>\n<p>Un personnage Lossoth est d’abord défini par sa communauté, son territoire de chasse et sa relation au Grand Nord. Un voyage vers le Sud constitue un changement considérable : abondance de bois, routes permanentes, villes et climats doux lui paraissent souvent aussi étranges que la banquise l’est à un Gondorien.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Langues de départ</h2><ul><li><strong>Labba</strong> — Parlée 8 / Écrite 0</li><li><strong>Westron</strong> — Parlée 4 / Écrite 2</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Parlée 4 / Écrite 2</li></ul></section>","culture":"Lossoth"}},"en":{"name":"Lossoth","system":{"description":"<h1>Lossoth</h1>\n<p>The <strong>Lossoth</strong> are the Men of the Far North who dwell around the Bay of Forochel. Their Culture was shaped in a land of tundra, snow, ice and violent winds where survival depends on intimate knowledge of the seasons, animals and movement across frozen ground. They belong to the <strong>Humans — Hildor</strong> Race and remain one of the peoples best adapted to the polar conditions of Middle-earth.</p>\n<h2>The Far North</h2>\n<p>Lossoth communities live according to the rhythm of freezing weather, animal migrations and the availability of resources. Camps, shelters and routes change with the seasons; families know how to recognise load-bearing snow, dangerous ice, signs of a storm and areas where game or fuel can be found.</p>\n<p>Cold is not merely a background feature but a permanent condition of life. Clothing, food, the organisation of travel and the division of tasks are all designed to avoid wasting heat or energy.</p>\n<h2>Appearance and adaptation</h2>\n<p>The Lossoth are generally sturdy and compact, with features adapted to an extreme climate. Their clothing layers hides, fur and leather to protect the body from wind and moisture. Their endurance against cold is remarkable, while very hot climates are far less familiar to them.</p>\n<h2>Hunting, fishing and husbandry</h2>\n<p>Hunting, fishing and trapping provide most resources. The Lossoth use meat, hides, bones and fat with very little waste. Dogs and reindeer hold an important place in some communities for transport, hauling or herding.</p>\n<p>Practical knowledge matters as much as strength: following a trail after snowfall, rapidly building shelter, preserving food or crossing a frozen expanse are ordinary skills.</p>\n<h2>Society and traditions</h2>\n<p>Family and the survival group take precedence over complex institutions. Elders are respected for their memory of winters, migrations and safe places. Keeping one's word and mutual aid carry particular weight in an environment where isolation can be deadly.</p>\n<p>Stories, songs and beliefs transmit the memory of ancestors, spirits, animals and natural phenomena. Religion remains closely tied to the visible world and to the forces that govern the North.</p>\n<h2>Travel and combat</h2>\n<p>The Lossoth excel at movement across snow, tracking, survival, weather observation and the use of equipment suited to cold. Their weapons remain functional: spears, javelins, bows, knives and hunting tools predominate. Mobility and knowledge of terrain matter more than heavy armour.</p>\n<h2>Place in character creation</h2>\n<p>A Lossoth character is defined first by community, hunting territory and relationship with the Far North. A journey south represents an enormous change: abundant timber, permanent roads, cities and mild climates often seem as strange to them as the pack ice does to a Gondorian.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Starting Languages</h2><ul><li><strong>Labba</strong> — Spoken 8 / Written 0</li><li><strong>Westron</strong> — Spoken 4 / Written 2</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Spoken 4 / Written 2</li></ul></section>","culture":"Lossoth"}}}}},"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":["Humains"],"en":["Humans"]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":["cultures-humans"],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"system":{"book":"MERP-RMU","table":"Conversion RMSS/RMFRP → RMU","culture":"Lossoth","description":"<h1>Lossoth</h1>\n<p>The <strong>Lossoth</strong> are the Men of the Far North who dwell around the Bay of Forochel. Their Culture was shaped in a land of tundra, snow, ice and violent winds where survival depends on intimate knowledge of the seasons, animals and movement across frozen ground. They belong to the <strong>Humans — Hildor</strong> Race and remain one of the peoples best adapted to the polar conditions of Middle-earth.</p>\n<h2>The Far North</h2>\n<p>Lossoth communities live according to the rhythm of freezing weather, animal migrations and the availability of resources. Camps, shelters and routes change with the seasons; families know how to recognise load-bearing snow, dangerous ice, signs of a storm and areas where game or fuel can be found.</p>\n<p>Cold is not merely a background feature but a permanent condition of life. Clothing, food, the organisation of travel and the division of tasks are all designed to avoid wasting heat or energy.</p>\n<h2>Appearance and adaptation</h2>\n<p>The Lossoth are generally sturdy and compact, with features adapted to an extreme climate. Their clothing layers hides, fur and leather to protect the body from wind and moisture. Their endurance against cold is remarkable, while very hot climates are far less familiar to them.</p>\n<h2>Hunting, fishing and husbandry</h2>\n<p>Hunting, fishing and trapping provide most resources. The Lossoth use meat, hides, bones and fat with very little waste. Dogs and reindeer hold an important place in some communities for transport, hauling or herding.</p>\n<p>Practical knowledge matters as much as strength: following a trail after snowfall, rapidly building shelter, preserving food or crossing a frozen expanse are ordinary skills.</p>\n<h2>Society and traditions</h2>\n<p>Family and the survival group take precedence over complex institutions. Elders are respected for their memory of winters, migrations and safe places. Keeping one's word and mutual aid carry particular weight in an environment where isolation can be deadly.</p>\n<p>Stories, songs and beliefs transmit the memory of ancestors, spirits, animals and natural phenomena. Religion remains closely tied to the visible world and to the forces that govern the North.</p>\n<h2>Travel and combat</h2>\n<p>The Lossoth excel at movement across snow, tracking, survival, weather observation and the use of equipment suited to cold. Their weapons remain functional: spears, javelins, bows, knives and hunting tools predominate. Mobility and knowledge of terrain matter more than heavy armour.</p>\n<h2>Place in character creation</h2>\n<p>A Lossoth character is defined first by community, hunting territory and relationship with the Far North. A journey south represents an enormous change: abundant timber, permanent roads, cities and mild climates often seem as strange to them as the pack ice does to a Gondorian.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Starting Languages</h2><ul><li><strong>Labba</strong> — Spoken 8 / Written 0</li><li><strong>Westron</strong> — Spoken 4 / Written 2</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Spoken 4 / Written 2</li></ul></section>","cultureRanks":[{"skillCategory":"Animal","skillName":"Animal Handling","ranks":3,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Animal","skillName":"Riding","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Awareness","skillName":"Perception","ranks":4},{"skillCategory":"Awareness","skillName":"Tracking","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Battle Expertise","skillName":"Maneuvering in Armor","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Brawn","skillName":"Body Development","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Brawn","skillName":"Weight Training","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Unarmed","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Melee Weapons","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Ranged Weapons","ranks":3,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Composition & Performance Art","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Crafting & Vocation","ranks":5,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Navigation","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Piloting","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Survival","specialization":"Coastlands","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Gymnastic","skillName":"Acrobatics","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Gymnastic","skillName":"Jumping","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Languages","ranks":8,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillName":"Region Lore","specialization":"Own","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillName":"Region Lore","specialization":"Neighboring","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Religion/Philosophy","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Other Lores","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Medical","skillName":"Herbalism","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Medical","skillName":"Medicine","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Climbing","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Running","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Swimming","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Influence","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Social Awareness","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Trading","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Subterfuge","skillName":"Concealment","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Subterfuge","skillName":"Stalking","ranks":3}]},"_id":"0teQd5tG7D5c1r3Q"}
{"name":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","type":"culture","img":"systems/rmu/icons/svg/iron_crown_w.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"key":"culture-luindrim","canonicalKey":"culture-luindrim","collection":"merp-rmu","contentVersion":1,"source":{"type":"merp-rmss-to-rmu-conversion","reference":"MERP Character Creation Using RMSS/RMFRP v2.5"},"raceCanonicalKey":"race-elves","availability":{"ages":[1,2,3,4],"restrictedByAge":{"1":false,"2":false,"3":false,"4":false}},"descriptionFormat":"html","compendiumCanonical":true,"ageVariants":{"1":{"sourceKey":"culture-luindrim-age-1","folderKey":"cultures-age-1-elves","document":{"name":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","type":"culture","img":"systems/rmu/icons/svg/iron_crown_w.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"key":"culture-luindrim-age-1","canonicalKey":"culture-luindrim","collection":"merp-rmu","contentVersion":1,"source":{"type":"merp-rmss-to-rmu-conversion","reference":"MERP Character Creation Using RMSS/RMFRP v2.5"},"raceKey":"race-elves-age-1","raceCanonicalKey":"race-elves","availability":{"age":1,"ageLabel":"Premier Âge","restricted":false},"descriptionFormat":"html","languages":{"starting":[{"name":"Luinbeth","spoken":10,"written":10,"nameFr":"Luinbeth"},{"name":"Sindarin","spoken":8,"written":6,"nameFr":"Sindarin"}],"source":"MERP Character Creation Using RMSS/RMFRP v2.5","sourceStatus":"verified"}}},"system":{"book":"MERP-RMU","table":"Conversion RMSS/RMFRP → RMU","culture":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","description":"<h1>Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith</h1>\n<p>Les <strong>Luindrim</strong> sont des Elfes <strong>Avari</strong> qui quittèrent Cuiviénen après le départ des Eldar et finirent par s’établir dans le pays de Luindor sous la conduite de Lindor. Ils se nomment aussi <strong>Foredhil</strong>, « Elfes du Nord », ou <strong>Iaurwaith</strong>, « Vieux Peuple ». Leur Culture associe vie forestière, petites communautés, artisanat du bois, musique et institutions politiques peu autoritaires.</p>\n<h2>Nature elfique</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim partagent l’immortalité, la résistance aux maladies, les sens aigus et la méditation des Quendi. Ils voient remarquablement bien sous les étoiles, se déplacent avec légèreté et sont particulièrement à l’aise dans les forêts et les régions enneigées.</p>\n<h2>Société</h2>\n<p>Le Roi et la Reine servent surtout d’arbitres, de gardiens des traditions et de figures cérémonielles. Le statut dépend davantage de la sagesse, de la compétence et de la maîtrise d’un métier que de la naissance.</p>\n<p>Forgerons, chasseurs, tisserands, guérisseurs et ménestrels forment des communautés professionnelles souples qui peuvent se réunir pour résoudre les problèmes liés à leur activité.</p>\n<h2>Villages et telain</h2>\n<p>Les villages utilisent deux niveaux. Au sol se trouvent entrepôts, écuries et petits bâtiments ; les principaux espaces de vie sont installés sur de grandes plates-formes de bois, les telain, intégrées aux arbres et parfois entourées de parois sculptées ou vitrées.</p>\n<h2>Vie quotidienne</h2>\n<p>Leur alimentation utilise produits laitiers, œufs, poisson, gibier et fruits cultivés parfois sous serre. Le bois, le cuir, le textile, l’empennage et la musique occupent une place importante. Les vêtements privilégient bleus, verts et jaunes profonds, avec des manteaux de camouflage pour les sorties.</p>\n<h2>Religion</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim révèrent les Valar de manière informelle. Ivannië, Araw et Elbereth sont particulièrement présents dans les fêtes saisonnières. La méditation et la célébration collective comptent davantage qu’une institution sacerdotale complexe.</p>\n<h2>Relations et guerre</h2>\n<p>Ils détestent les Orcs et les Hommes d’Urd, évitent souvent les Umli et entretiennent des relations commerciales avec certains Khazâd. Leur manière de combattre exploite la forêt, la Dissimulation, l’Embuscade et le tir à distance, tout en permettant une grande variété d’armes et d’armures.</p>\n<h2>Place dans la création de personnage</h2>\n<p>Un Luindrim doit être rattaché à une communauté de Luindor et à un métier ou domaine de maîtrise. Sa liberté personnelle, son ancienneté avarine et sa relation avec les institutions souples du royaume donnent une identité très différente de celle des Elfes occidentaux.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Langues de départ</h2><ul><li><strong>Luinbeth</strong> — Parlée 10 / Écrite 10</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Parlée 8 / Écrite 6</li></ul></section>","cultureRanks":[{"skillCategory":"Animal","skillName":"Animal Handling","ranks":1,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Animal","skillName":"Riding","ranks":1,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Awareness","skillName":"Perception","ranks":5},{"skillCategory":"Awareness","skillName":"Tracking","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Battle Expertise","skillName":"Maneuvering in Armor","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Brawn","skillName":"Body Development","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Brawn","skillName":"Weight Training","ranks":0},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Unarmed","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Melee Weapons","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Ranged Weapons","ranks":4,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Composition & Performance Art","ranks":6,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Crafting & Vocation","ranks":6,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Navigation","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Piloting","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Survival","specialization":"Forest","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Gymnastic","skillName":"Acrobatics","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Gymnastic","skillName":"Jumping","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Languages","ranks":10,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillName":"Region Lore","specialization":"Own","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillName":"Region Lore","specialization":"Neighboring","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Religion/Philosophy","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Other Lores","ranks":0,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Medical","skillName":"Herbalism","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Medical","skillName":"Medicine","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Climbing","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Running","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Swimming","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Influence","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Social Awareness","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Trading","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Subterfuge","skillName":"Concealment","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Subterfuge","skillName":"Stalking","ranks":3}]}},"localizations":{"fr":{"name":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","system":{"description":"<h1>Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith</h1>\n<p>Les <strong>Luindrim</strong> sont des Elfes <strong>Avari</strong> qui quittèrent Cuiviénen après le départ des Eldar et finirent par s’établir dans le pays de Luindor sous la conduite de Lindor. Ils se nomment aussi <strong>Foredhil</strong>, « Elfes du Nord », ou <strong>Iaurwaith</strong>, « Vieux Peuple ». Leur Culture associe vie forestière, petites communautés, artisanat du bois, musique et institutions politiques peu autoritaires.</p>\n<h2>Nature elfique</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim partagent l’immortalité, la résistance aux maladies, les sens aigus et la méditation des Quendi. Ils voient remarquablement bien sous les étoiles, se déplacent avec légèreté et sont particulièrement à l’aise dans les forêts et les régions enneigées.</p>\n<h2>Société</h2>\n<p>Le Roi et la Reine servent surtout d’arbitres, de gardiens des traditions et de figures cérémonielles. Le statut dépend davantage de la sagesse, de la compétence et de la maîtrise d’un métier que de la naissance.</p>\n<p>Forgerons, chasseurs, tisserands, guérisseurs et ménestrels forment des communautés professionnelles souples qui peuvent se réunir pour résoudre les problèmes liés à leur activité.</p>\n<h2>Villages et telain</h2>\n<p>Les villages utilisent deux niveaux. Au sol se trouvent entrepôts, écuries et petits bâtiments ; les principaux espaces de vie sont installés sur de grandes plates-formes de bois, les telain, intégrées aux arbres et parfois entourées de parois sculptées ou vitrées.</p>\n<h2>Vie quotidienne</h2>\n<p>Leur alimentation utilise produits laitiers, œufs, poisson, gibier et fruits cultivés parfois sous serre. Le bois, le cuir, le textile, l’empennage et la musique occupent une place importante. Les vêtements privilégient bleus, verts et jaunes profonds, avec des manteaux de camouflage pour les sorties.</p>\n<h2>Religion</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim révèrent les Valar de manière informelle. Ivannië, Araw et Elbereth sont particulièrement présents dans les fêtes saisonnières. La méditation et la célébration collective comptent davantage qu’une institution sacerdotale complexe.</p>\n<h2>Relations et guerre</h2>\n<p>Ils détestent les Orcs et les Hommes d’Urd, évitent souvent les Umli et entretiennent des relations commerciales avec certains Khazâd. Leur manière de combattre exploite la forêt, la Dissimulation, l’Embuscade et le tir à distance, tout en permettant une grande variété d’armes et d’armures.</p>\n<h2>Place dans la création de personnage</h2>\n<p>Un Luindrim doit être rattaché à une communauté de Luindor et à un métier ou domaine de maîtrise. Sa liberté personnelle, son ancienneté avarine et sa relation avec les institutions souples du royaume donnent une identité très différente de celle des Elfes occidentaux.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Langues de départ</h2><ul><li><strong>Luinbeth</strong> — Parlée 10 / Écrite 10</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Parlée 8 / Écrite 6</li></ul></section>","culture":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith"}},"en":{"name":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","system":{"description":"<h1>Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith</h1>\n<p>The <strong>Luindrim</strong> are <strong>Avari</strong> Elves who left Cuiviénen after the departure of the Eldar and eventually settled in the land of Luindor under the leadership of Lindor. They also call themselves <strong>Foredhil</strong>, “Elves of the North”, or <strong>Iaurwaith</strong>, “Old People”. Their Culture combines woodland life, small communities, woodcraft, music and political institutions with little authoritarianism.</p>\n<h2>Elven nature</h2>\n<p>The Luindrim share the immortality, resistance to disease, keen senses and meditation of the Quendi. They see remarkably well beneath the stars, move lightly and are especially at ease in forests and snowy regions.</p>\n<h2>Society</h2>\n<p>The King and Queen serve chiefly as arbiters, guardians of tradition and ceremonial figures. Status depends more on wisdom, competence and mastery of a craft than on birth.</p>\n<p>Smiths, hunters, weavers, healers and minstrels form flexible professional communities that may gather to solve problems related to their work.</p>\n<h2>Villages and telain</h2>\n<p>Villages use two levels. Storehouses, stables and small buildings stand on the ground; the principal living spaces are built upon large wooden platforms, the telain, integrated into the trees and sometimes surrounded by carved or glazed walls.</p>\n<h2>Daily life</h2>\n<p>Their diet makes use of dairy products, eggs, fish, game and fruit, sometimes cultivated under glass. Wood, leather, textiles, fletching and music all hold an important place. Clothing favours deep blues, greens and yellows, with camouflage cloaks for excursions.</p>\n<h2>Religion</h2>\n<p>The Luindrim revere the Valar informally. Ivannië, Araw and Elbereth are especially prominent in seasonal festivals. Meditation and communal celebration matter more than a complex priestly institution.</p>\n<h2>Relations and warfare</h2>\n<p>They hate Orcs and the Men of Urd, often avoid the Umli and maintain trading relations with certain Khazâd. Their fighting style exploits forest, Concealment, Ambush and missile fire while allowing a wide variety of weapons and armour.</p>\n<h2>Place in character creation</h2>\n<p>A Luindrim should be tied to a community of Luindor and to a craft or field of mastery. Their personal freedom, ancient Avarin heritage and relationship with the kingdom's flexible institutions give them an identity very different from that of western Elves.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Starting Languages</h2><ul><li><strong>Luinbeth</strong> — Spoken 10 / Written 10</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Spoken 8 / Written 6</li></ul></section>","culture":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith"}}}},"2":{"sourceKey":"culture-luindrim-age-2","folderKey":"cultures-age-2-elves","document":{"name":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","type":"culture","img":"systems/rmu/icons/svg/iron_crown_w.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"key":"culture-luindrim-age-2","canonicalKey":"culture-luindrim","collection":"merp-rmu","contentVersion":1,"source":{"type":"merp-rmss-to-rmu-conversion","reference":"MERP Character Creation Using RMSS/RMFRP v2.5"},"raceKey":"race-elves-age-2","raceCanonicalKey":"race-elves","availability":{"age":2,"ageLabel":"Deuxième Âge","restricted":false},"descriptionFormat":"html","languages":{"starting":[{"name":"Luinbeth","spoken":10,"written":10,"nameFr":"Luinbeth"},{"name":"Sindarin","spoken":8,"written":6,"nameFr":"Sindarin"}],"source":"MERP Character Creation Using RMSS/RMFRP v2.5","sourceStatus":"verified"}}},"system":{"book":"MERP-RMU","table":"Conversion RMSS/RMFRP → RMU","culture":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","description":"<h1>Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith</h1>\n<p>Les <strong>Luindrim</strong> sont des Elfes <strong>Avari</strong> qui quittèrent Cuiviénen après le départ des Eldar et finirent par s’établir dans le pays de Luindor sous la conduite de Lindor. Ils se nomment aussi <strong>Foredhil</strong>, « Elfes du Nord », ou <strong>Iaurwaith</strong>, « Vieux Peuple ». Leur Culture associe vie forestière, petites communautés, artisanat du bois, musique et institutions politiques peu autoritaires.</p>\n<h2>Nature elfique</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim partagent l’immortalité, la résistance aux maladies, les sens aigus et la méditation des Quendi. Ils voient remarquablement bien sous les étoiles, se déplacent avec légèreté et sont particulièrement à l’aise dans les forêts et les régions enneigées.</p>\n<h2>Société</h2>\n<p>Le Roi et la Reine servent surtout d’arbitres, de gardiens des traditions et de figures cérémonielles. Le statut dépend davantage de la sagesse, de la compétence et de la maîtrise d’un métier que de la naissance.</p>\n<p>Forgerons, chasseurs, tisserands, guérisseurs et ménestrels forment des communautés professionnelles souples qui peuvent se réunir pour résoudre les problèmes liés à leur activité.</p>\n<h2>Villages et telain</h2>\n<p>Les villages utilisent deux niveaux. Au sol se trouvent entrepôts, écuries et petits bâtiments ; les principaux espaces de vie sont installés sur de grandes plates-formes de bois, les telain, intégrées aux arbres et parfois entourées de parois sculptées ou vitrées.</p>\n<h2>Vie quotidienne</h2>\n<p>Leur alimentation utilise produits laitiers, œufs, poisson, gibier et fruits cultivés parfois sous serre. Le bois, le cuir, le textile, l’empennage et la musique occupent une place importante. Les vêtements privilégient bleus, verts et jaunes profonds, avec des manteaux de camouflage pour les sorties.</p>\n<h2>Religion</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim révèrent les Valar de manière informelle. Ivannië, Araw et Elbereth sont particulièrement présents dans les fêtes saisonnières. La méditation et la célébration collective comptent davantage qu’une institution sacerdotale complexe.</p>\n<h2>Relations et guerre</h2>\n<p>Ils détestent les Orcs et les Hommes d’Urd, évitent souvent les Umli et entretiennent des relations commerciales avec certains Khazâd. Leur manière de combattre exploite la forêt, la Dissimulation, l’Embuscade et le tir à distance, tout en permettant une grande variété d’armes et d’armures.</p>\n<h2>Place dans la création de personnage</h2>\n<p>Un Luindrim doit être rattaché à une communauté de Luindor et à un métier ou domaine de maîtrise. Sa liberté personnelle, son ancienneté avarine et sa relation avec les institutions souples du royaume donnent une identité très différente de celle des Elfes occidentaux.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Langues de départ</h2><ul><li><strong>Luinbeth</strong> — Parlée 10 / Écrite 10</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Parlée 8 / Écrite 6</li></ul></section>","cultureRanks":[{"skillCategory":"Animal","skillName":"Animal Handling","ranks":1,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Animal","skillName":"Riding","ranks":1,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Awareness","skillName":"Perception","ranks":5},{"skillCategory":"Awareness","skillName":"Tracking","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Battle Expertise","skillName":"Maneuvering in Armor","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Brawn","skillName":"Body Development","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Brawn","skillName":"Weight Training","ranks":0},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Unarmed","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Melee Weapons","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Ranged Weapons","ranks":4,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Composition & Performance Art","ranks":6,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Crafting & Vocation","ranks":6,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Navigation","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Piloting","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Survival","specialization":"Forest","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Gymnastic","skillName":"Acrobatics","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Gymnastic","skillName":"Jumping","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Languages","ranks":10,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillName":"Region Lore","specialization":"Own","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillName":"Region Lore","specialization":"Neighboring","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Religion/Philosophy","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Other Lores","ranks":0,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Medical","skillName":"Herbalism","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Medical","skillName":"Medicine","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Climbing","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Running","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Swimming","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Influence","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Social Awareness","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillName":"Trading","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Subterfuge","skillName":"Concealment","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Subterfuge","skillName":"Stalking","ranks":3}]}},"localizations":{"fr":{"name":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","system":{"description":"<h1>Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith</h1>\n<p>Les <strong>Luindrim</strong> sont des Elfes <strong>Avari</strong> qui quittèrent Cuiviénen après le départ des Eldar et finirent par s’établir dans le pays de Luindor sous la conduite de Lindor. Ils se nomment aussi <strong>Foredhil</strong>, « Elfes du Nord », ou <strong>Iaurwaith</strong>, « Vieux Peuple ». Leur Culture associe vie forestière, petites communautés, artisanat du bois, musique et institutions politiques peu autoritaires.</p>\n<h2>Nature elfique</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim partagent l’immortalité, la résistance aux maladies, les sens aigus et la méditation des Quendi. Ils voient remarquablement bien sous les étoiles, se déplacent avec légèreté et sont particulièrement à l’aise dans les forêts et les régions enneigées.</p>\n<h2>Société</h2>\n<p>Le Roi et la Reine servent surtout d’arbitres, de gardiens des traditions et de figures cérémonielles. Le statut dépend davantage de la sagesse, de la compétence et de la maîtrise d’un métier que de la naissance.</p>\n<p>Forgerons, chasseurs, tisserands, guérisseurs et ménestrels forment des communautés professionnelles souples qui peuvent se réunir pour résoudre les problèmes liés à leur activité.</p>\n<h2>Villages et telain</h2>\n<p>Les villages utilisent deux niveaux. Au sol se trouvent entrepôts, écuries et petits bâtiments ; les principaux espaces de vie sont installés sur de grandes plates-formes de bois, les telain, intégrées aux arbres et parfois entourées de parois sculptées ou vitrées.</p>\n<h2>Vie quotidienne</h2>\n<p>Leur alimentation utilise produits laitiers, œufs, poisson, gibier et fruits cultivés parfois sous serre. Le bois, le cuir, le textile, l’empennage et la musique occupent une place importante. Les vêtements privilégient bleus, verts et jaunes profonds, avec des manteaux de camouflage pour les sorties.</p>\n<h2>Religion</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim révèrent les Valar de manière informelle. Ivannië, Araw et Elbereth sont particulièrement présents dans les fêtes saisonnières. La méditation et la célébration collective comptent davantage qu’une institution sacerdotale complexe.</p>\n<h2>Relations et guerre</h2>\n<p>Ils détestent les Orcs et les Hommes d’Urd, évitent souvent les Umli et entretiennent des relations commerciales avec certains Khazâd. Leur manière de combattre exploite la forêt, la Dissimulation, l’Embuscade et le tir à distance, tout en permettant une grande variété d’armes et d’armures.</p>\n<h2>Place dans la création de personnage</h2>\n<p>Un Luindrim doit être rattaché à une communauté de Luindor et à un métier ou domaine de maîtrise. Sa liberté personnelle, son ancienneté avarine et sa relation avec les institutions souples du royaume donnent une identité très différente de celle des Elfes occidentaux.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Langues de départ</h2><ul><li><strong>Luinbeth</strong> — Parlée 10 / Écrite 10</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Parlée 8 / Écrite 6</li></ul></section>","culture":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith"}},"en":{"name":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","system":{"description":"<h1>Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith</h1>\n<p>The <strong>Luindrim</strong> are <strong>Avari</strong> Elves who left Cuiviénen after the departure of the Eldar and eventually settled in the land of Luindor under the leadership of Lindor. They also call themselves <strong>Foredhil</strong>, “Elves of the North”, or <strong>Iaurwaith</strong>, “Old People”. Their Culture combines woodland life, small communities, woodcraft, music and political institutions with little authoritarianism.</p>\n<h2>Elven nature</h2>\n<p>The Luindrim share the immortality, resistance to disease, keen senses and meditation of the Quendi. They see remarkably well beneath the stars, move lightly and are especially at ease in forests and snowy regions.</p>\n<h2>Society</h2>\n<p>The King and Queen serve chiefly as arbiters, guardians of tradition and ceremonial figures. Status depends more on wisdom, competence and mastery of a craft than on birth.</p>\n<p>Smiths, hunters, weavers, healers and minstrels form flexible professional communities that may gather to solve problems related to their work.</p>\n<h2>Villages and telain</h2>\n<p>Villages use two levels. Storehouses, stables and small buildings stand on the ground; the principal living spaces are built upon large wooden platforms, the telain, integrated into the trees and sometimes surrounded by carved or glazed walls.</p>\n<h2>Daily life</h2>\n<p>Their diet makes use of dairy products, eggs, fish, game and fruit, sometimes cultivated under glass. Wood, leather, textiles, fletching and music all hold an important place. Clothing favours deep blues, greens and yellows, with camouflage cloaks for excursions.</p>\n<h2>Religion</h2>\n<p>The Luindrim revere the Valar informally. Ivannië, Araw and Elbereth are especially prominent in seasonal festivals. Meditation and communal celebration matter more than a complex priestly institution.</p>\n<h2>Relations and warfare</h2>\n<p>They hate Orcs and the Men of Urd, often avoid the Umli and maintain trading relations with certain Khazâd. Their fighting style exploits forest, Concealment, Ambush and missile fire while allowing a wide variety of weapons and armour.</p>\n<h2>Place in character creation</h2>\n<p>A Luindrim should be tied to a community of Luindor and to a craft or field of mastery. Their personal freedom, ancient Avarin heritage and relationship with the kingdom's flexible institutions give them an identity very different from that of western Elves.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Starting Languages</h2><ul><li><strong>Luinbeth</strong> — Spoken 10 / Written 10</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Spoken 8 / Written 6</li></ul></section>","culture":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith"}}}},"3":{"sourceKey":"culture-luindrim-age-3","folderKey":"cultures-age-3-elves","document":{"name":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","type":"culture","img":"systems/rmu/icons/svg/iron_crown_w.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"key":"culture-luindrim-age-3","canonicalKey":"culture-luindrim","collection":"merp-rmu","contentVersion":1,"source":{"type":"merp-rmss-to-rmu-conversion","reference":"MERP Character Creation Using RMSS/RMFRP v2.5"},"raceKey":"race-elves-age-3","raceCanonicalKey":"race-elves","availability":{"age":3,"ageLabel":"Troisième Âge","restricted":false},"descriptionFormat":"html","languages":{"starting":[{"name":"Luinbeth","spoken":10,"written":10,"nameFr":"Luinbeth"},{"name":"Sindarin","spoken":8,"written":6,"nameFr":"Sindarin"}],"source":"MERP Character Creation Using RMSS/RMFRP v2.5","sourceStatus":"verified"}}},"system":{"book":"MERP-RMU","table":"Conversion RMSS/RMFRP → RMU","culture":"Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith","description":"<h1>Luindrim — Foredhil / Iaurwaith</h1>\n<p>Les <strong>Luindrim</strong> sont des Elfes <strong>Avari</strong> qui quittèrent Cuiviénen après le départ des Eldar et finirent par s’établir dans le pays de Luindor sous la conduite de Lindor. Ils se nomment aussi <strong>Foredhil</strong>, « Elfes du Nord », ou <strong>Iaurwaith</strong>, « Vieux Peuple ». Leur Culture associe vie forestière, petites communautés, artisanat du bois, musique et institutions politiques peu autoritaires.</p>\n<h2>Nature elfique</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim partagent l’immortalité, la résistance aux maladies, les sens aigus et la méditation des Quendi. Ils voient remarquablement bien sous les étoiles, se déplacent avec légèreté et sont particulièrement à l’aise dans les forêts et les régions enneigées.</p>\n<h2>Société</h2>\n<p>Le Roi et la Reine servent surtout d’arbitres, de gardiens des traditions et de figures cérémonielles. Le statut dépend davantage de la sagesse, de la compétence et de la maîtrise d’un métier que de la naissance.</p>\n<p>Forgerons, chasseurs, tisserands, guérisseurs et ménestrels forment des communautés professionnelles souples qui peuvent se réunir pour résoudre les problèmes liés à leur activité.</p>\n<h2>Villages et telain</h2>\n<p>Les villages utilisent deux niveaux. Au sol se trouvent entrepôts, écuries et petits bâtiments ; les principaux espaces de vie sont installés sur de grandes plates-formes de bois, les telain, intégrées aux arbres et parfois entourées de parois sculptées ou vitrées.</p>\n<h2>Vie quotidienne</h2>\n<p>Leur alimentation utilise produits laitiers, œufs, poisson, gibier et fruits cultivés parfois sous serre. Le bois, le cuir, le textile, l’empennage et la musique occupent une place importante. Les vêtements privilégient bleus, verts et jaunes profonds, avec des manteaux de camouflage pour les sorties.</p>\n<h2>Religion</h2>\n<p>Les Luindrim révèrent les Valar de manière informelle. Ivannië, Araw et Elbereth sont particulièrement présents dans les fêtes saisonnières. La méditation et la célébration collective comptent davantage qu’une institution sacerdotale complexe.</p>\n<h2>Relations et guerre</h2>\n<p>Ils détestent les Orcs et les Hommes d’Urd, évitent souvent les Umli et entretiennent des relations commerciales avec certains Khazâd. Leur manière de combattre exploite la forêt, la Dissimulation, l’Embuscade et le tir à distance, tout en permettant une grande variété d’armes et d’armures.</p>\n<h2>Place dans la création de personnage</h2>\n<p>Un Luindrim doit être rattaché à une communauté de Luindor et à un métier ou domaine de maîtrise. Sa liberté personnelle, son ancienneté avarine et sa relation avec les institutions souples du royaume donnent une identité très différente de celle des Elfes occidentaux.</p><section class=\"merp-ui-starting-languages\" data-merp-ui-starting-languages=\"1\"><h2>Langues de départ</h2><ul><li><strong>Luinbeth</strong> — Parlée 10 / Écrite 10</li><li><strong>Sindarin</strong> — Parlée 8 / Écrite 6</li></ul></section>","cultureRanks":[{"skillCategory":"Animal","skillName":"Animal Handling","ranks":1,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Animal","skillName":"Riding","ranks":1,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Awareness","skillName":"Perception","ranks":5},{"skillCategory":"Awareness","skillName":"Tracking","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Battle Expertise","skillName":"Maneuvering in Armor","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Brawn","skillName":"Body Development","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Brawn","skillName":"Weight Training","ranks":0},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Unarmed","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Melee Weapons","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Combat Training","skillGroup":"Ranged Weapons","ranks":4,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Composition & Performance Art","ranks":6,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Crafting & Vocation","ranks":6,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Navigation","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Piloting","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Environmental","skillName":"Survival","specialization":"Forest","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Gymnastic","skillName":"Acrobatics","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Gymnastic","skillName":"Jumping","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Languages","ranks":10,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillName":"Region Lore","specialization":"Own","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillName":"Region Lore","specialization":"Neighboring","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Religion/Philosophy","ranks":2,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Lore","skillGroup":"Other Lores","ranks":0,"maxTwoRanksPerSpecialization":true},{"skillCategory":"Medical","skillName":"Herbalism","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Medical","skillName":"Medicine","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Climbing","ranks":3},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Running","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Movement","skillName":"Swimming","ranks":2},{"skillCategory":"Social","skillN